\description{
Global heterogeneity \eqn{H = K^{-1}\sum_k\|W_k - \bar W\|_F^2} (inertia of the interstructure), its value relative to the mean of the \eqn{\|W_k\|_F^2}, the RV-based index \eqn{1 - \lambda_1(RV)/K}, and, when components are given, the share of \eqn{H} reproduced by each of them, \eqn{V(u_r)/H}. For any orthonormal set of components these shares add up to at most 1.
}
